#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Internet relay chat"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "សេចក្ដី​ណែនាំ"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ksirc; is the default &kde; &irc; client. It supports scripting with <acronym>"
"Perl</acronym> and has a lot of compatibility with &mirc; for general use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &ksirc;"
msgstr "ដោយ​ប្រើ Ksirc"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you haven't used &irc; before..."
msgstr "បើ​អ្នក​មិន​ធ្លាប់​បាន​ប្រើ IRC ពី​មុន..."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply put, &irc; is a chat protocol, defined by official Internet standards, "
"and capable of stealing many hours of your life. To use &irc;, you must connect "
"to a server, and then join a channel (equivalent to a chat room)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To connect to a server, open &ksirc; and select <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"Connections</guimenu><guimenuitem>New Server...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"or press <keycap>F2</keycap>. In the dialog box that is displayed, select a "
"group from the leftmost drop-down box and then a server from the middle "
"drop-down box. The port, shown on the right, will almost always be 6667. A new "
"window will be displayed showing the messages sent by the server to the client. "
"When these messages have finished scrolling past, you want to choose your "
"channel. To display a list of available channels, type <userinput><command>"
"/list</command></userinput>. To join a channel, type: <userinput><command>"
"/join</command> <replaceable>#channelname</replaceable></userinput>"
". To leave a channel, just type <userinput><command>/part</command></userinput>"
"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "That's the basics; for more detailed information, read on..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ksirc; Basics"
msgstr "Ksirc​ មូលដ្ឋាន"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "Servers"
msgstr "ម៉ាស៊ីន​បម្រើ"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ksirc; allows you to connect to any number of servers. To connect to a server, "
"select <menuchoice><guimenu>Connections</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"New Server</guimenuitem></menuchoice> or press <keycap>F2</keycap>"
".The <guilabel>Connect to Server</guilabel> Dialog appears, and you can select "
"a <guilabel>Group</guilabel>, then a <guilabel>Server</guilabel>"
", and also a <guilabel>Port</guilabel> to connect to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Just click <guilabel>Connect</guilabel> when you're done, and a new window for "
"the server is displayed. You can keep track of the servers you're connected to "
"in the &ksirc; <guilabel>Server Control</guilabel> window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can get help on most &irc; commands by typing <userinput>/help <replaceable>"
"commandname</replaceable></userinput>. Typing <userinput>/help</userinput> "
"on its own gives a list of available commands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:136 index.docbook:675
#, no-c-format
msgid "Channels"
msgstr "ឆានែល"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can connect to channels with the normal &irc; command <userinput><command>"
"/join</command> <replaceable>#channelname</replaceable> </userinput>"
", by selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Connections</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Join Channel...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> or by pressing <keycap>F3</keycap>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Channels you are connected to are shown in the <guilabel>"
"Server Control</guilabel> window under the server to which the they belong. To "
"leave a channel, you can <userinput>/part</userinput>, select <menuchoice>"
"<guimenu>Channel</guimenu><guimenuitem>Close</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> "
"or press <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>W</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "Channel Options"
msgstr "ជម្រើស​ឆានែល"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenu>Channel</guimenu> menu, available in any channel window, contains "
"some useful options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>S</keycap> </keycombo></shortcut> "
"<guimenuitem>Save to Logfile...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saves the contents of the channel to a file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenuitem>Time Stamp</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If selected, prepends each thing said in the channel with the time it was said, "
"in the form [HH:MM:SS]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"seq\">&Alt;<keycap>C</keycap> <keycap>T</keycap>"
"</keycombo></shortcut> <guimenuitem>Ascii Table</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Displays a table of Ascii characters</action>"
", from which you can choose any characters you require."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"seq\">&Alt;<keycap>C</keycap> <keycap>P</keycap>"
"</keycombo></shortcut> <guimenuitem>Beep on Change</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "If selected, &ksirc; emits a beep every time something is said on a channel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In a channel, the user list is displayed along the right hand side. "
"Right-clicking a nickname in that list gives you a pop-up menu of options, most "
"of which are self-explanatory. Those actions can be configured (changing the "
"order, adding or removing some) in the Configure KSirc... dialog in the User "
"Menu tab. The default actions are the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid "Refresh Nicks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Sends a message to the server to request the list of users in the "
"channel.</action> This ensures that the list of nicknames is up-to-date."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Follow"
msgstr "ធ្វើ​តាម"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Highlights the user's nick in every message they send to the channel. This way, "
"you can follow someone's thread of conversation in a busy channel. The user's "
"nick color is picked at random."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "unFollow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stops following the user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Whois"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sends a &CTCP; whois query to the user, which provides information about the "
"user, such as his hostname and what server he is connected to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ping"
msgstr "ភីង"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sends a &CTCP; ping request to the user, to determine his echo time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "Version"
msgstr "កំណែ"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sends a &CTCP; version request to the user, to determine what software he is "
"using."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "Abuse"
msgstr "រំលោភ​ច្បាប់"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid "Abuses the user in one of various amusing ways."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following commands are only available if you are an operator on the "
"channel:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kick"
msgstr "ទាត់"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removes the user off the channel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenuitem>Ban</guimenuitem>"
msgstr "<guimenuitem>ហាម​ឃាត់</guimenuitem>"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bans the user from joining the channel."
msgstr "ហាម​ឃាត់​អ្នក​ប្រើ​ពី​ការ​ចូល​រួម​ប៉ុស្តិ៍ ។"

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "unBan"
msgstr "មិន​ហាម​ឃាត់"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removes the ban on the user joining the channel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenuitem>Op</guimenuitem>"
msgstr "<guimenuitem>Op</guimenuitem>"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gives the user operator privileges."
msgstr "ផ្ដល់​សិទ្ធិ​ការី​ទៅ​អ្នក​ប្រើ ។"

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid "DeOp"
msgstr "DeOp"

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removes operator privileges from the user."
msgstr "យក​ចេញ​សិទ្ធិ​ការី​ពី​អ្នក​ប្រើ ។"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid "Autoconnecting"
msgstr "ភ្ជាប់​ដោយ​ស្វ័យ​ប្រវត្តិ"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have a number of servers and/or channels which you connect to every time "
"you use &ksirc;, then you can set up &ksirc; to automatically connect to them: "
"In the <guilabel>Server Control</guilabel> window, select <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure KSirc...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
", and in the dialog which appears, select the <guilabel>Auto Connect</guilabel> "
"page. To add a channel on a new server, fill in the <guilabel>Server</guilabel> "
"and <guilabel>Channel</guilabel> text boxes, and then click on <guibutton>"
"Add</guibutton>. To add another channel on this server, select the server name "
"in the tree view, enter the channel name in the <guilabel>Channel</guilabel> "
"text box, and click on <guibutton>Update/Add</guibutton>"
". You can repeat this process as many times as you like to add several servers "
"and channels for &ksirc; to connect to at startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ksirc; Configuration"
msgstr "ការ​កំណត់​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ Ksirc"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction to Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &ksirc; configuration dialog is available from <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"Options</guimenu><guimenuitem>Preferences...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"in the &ksirc; <guilabel>Server Control</guilabel> window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:353
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Look and Feel</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid "Window Mode"
msgstr "របៀប​បង្អួច"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "SDI Mode (old behavior)"
msgstr "របៀប SDI (ឥរិយាបថ​ចាស់)"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Causes &ksirc; to use single document interface mode, in which each new channel "
"or <command>/query</command> window has its own, separate window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid "Paged MDI mode (XChat)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Causes &ksirc; to use multiple document interface mode, in the style of "
"<application>XChat</application>, in which each new channel or <command>"
"/query</command> window has a tab in one main &ksirc; window. Each tab can be "
"brought to the front by clicking its tab, and you can switch tabs using "
"<keycombo>&Alt;<keysym>Left Arrow</keysym></keycombo> and <keycombo>"
"&Alt;<keysym>Right Arrow</keysym></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wallpaper"
msgstr "ផ្ទាំង​រូបភាព"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Wallpaper</guilabel> section, you can change the image placed "
"in the background of your &ksirc; windows. You can enter the name of the file "
"to use in the text box, or browse for files using the button to the right of "
"the textbox. Image files used must be in &GIF;, <acronym>JPEG</acronym> "
"or <acronym>PNG</acronym> format. A preview of the image is shown at the right "
"of the dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you don't want a wallpaper, simply right-click in the path field and choose "
"clear in the context menu. Or remove the wallpaper location to leave the field "
"empty and click Apply. No wall paper will be set then."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>General</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr "ផ្ទាំង <guilabel>ទូទៅ</guilabel>"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid "Global Options"
msgstr "ជម្រើស​សកល"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dock in system tray"
msgstr "ចូល​ចត​ក្នុង​ថាស​ប្រព័ន្ធ"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This allows KSirc to be docked in the system tray. By default this is not "
"enabled. When KSirc is docked in the system tray, you are able to access "
"several options by clicking on the KSirc icon. When you close KSirc window, the "
"icon stays in the systray until you quit KSirc."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color picker popup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If selected, a popup window from which to select the color of your text is "
"presented when you press <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>K</keycap>"
"</keycombo>. If not, you have to type the color codes manually. See also <xref "
"linkend=\"sectcolors\"/>. This option is selected by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto create window"
msgstr "បង្កើត​បង្អួច​ដោយ​ស្វ័យ​ប្រវត្តិ"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If selected, &ksirc; will automatically create a new window for each user who "
"sends a <command>/msg</command> command to you. If not selected, any text sent "
"to you with <command>/msg</command> is displayed in the current window and you "
"can use <command>/query <replaceable>username</replaceable></command> "
"to create a window to chat to that user. It is selected by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto-rejoin"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:427
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rejoins channels automatically if you are disconnected."
msgstr "ចូល​រួម​ប៉ុស្តិ៍​ឡើង​វិញ​ស្វ័យ​ប្រវត្តិ បើ​អ្នក​ត្រូវ​បាន​ផ្ដាច់ ។"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto create on notice"
msgstr "បង្កើត​ចំណាំ​ស្វ័យ​ប្រវត្តិ"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If someone sends you a /notice then if this option is checked it will create a "
"new window."
msgstr "បើ​អ្នក​ណា​ម្នាក់​ផ្ញើ​អ្នក​នូវ /notice ហើយ​បើ​ជម្រើស​នេះ​ត្រូវ​បាន​ធីក វា​នឹង​បង្កើត​បង្អួច​ថ្មី ។"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "Announce away messages"
msgstr "ប្រកាស​សារ​ចាក​ឆ្ងាយ"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is checked, you will see the messages when a user selects the away "
"option. By default this option is not checked. It is checked by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid "Nick completion"
msgstr "ការ​បំពេញ​សម្មិតិ​នាម"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If selected, switches nickname completion on. Nickname completion works as "
"follows:"
msgstr "បើ​ជ្រើស បើក​ការ​បំពេញ​សម្មិតិ​នាម ។ ការ​បំពេញ​សម្មិតិនាម​ធ្វើការ​ដូច​ខាងក្រោម ៖"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid "Type the first letters of a user's nickname."
msgstr "វាយ​តួ​អក្សរ​ដំបូង​នៃ​សម្មិតិ​នាម​របស់​អ្នក​ប្រើ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press <keysym>TAB</keysym>. The text you typed will be completed to match the "
"username, including changes in capitalization if necessary. &eg; <userinput>"
"phi&lt;TAB&gt;</userinput> becomes <computeroutput>PhilRod</computeroutput> "
"if there is a user called <quote>PhilRod</quote> on the channel."
msgstr ""
"វាយ <keysym>TAB</keysym> ។ អត្ថបទ​ដែល​អ្នក​វា នឹង​ត្រូវ​បាន​បំពេញ​ដើម្បី​ផ្គូផ្គង​ឈ្មោះ​អ្នក​ប្រើ រួម​បញ្ចូល​ទាំង​ការ​ផ្លាស់ប្ដូរ​តួ​អក្សរ​ធំ បើ​ចាំ​បាច់ ។ ឧ. <userinput>"
"phi&lt;TAB&gt;</userinput> ក្លាយ​ជា <computeroutput>PhilRod</computeroutput> "
"បើ​មាន​អ្នក​ប្រើ​ត្រូវ​បាន​ហៅ <quote>PhilRod</quote> នៅ​លើ​ប៉ុស្តិ៍ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If more than one user's nickname on the channel matches the text you have "
"typed, the first name in the list is chosen. Pressing <keysym>TAB</keysym> "
"subsequent times displays the next nickname in the list. For example, if there "
"are users <quote>PhilA</quote> and <quote>PhilRod</quote> "
"on a channel, and you type <userinput>phi&lt;TAB&gt;</userinput>"
", the text will first be completed to <computeroutput>PhilA</computeroutput>"
", and if you press <keysym>TAB</keysym> again, it will change to "
"<computeroutput>PhilRod</computeroutput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use color nick list"
msgstr "ប្រើ​បញ្ជី​សម្មិតិ​ពណ៌"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If selected, it will use the colors set in the Colors tab of the Configure "
"KSirc dialog for coloring the nicknames."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid "Display topic in caption"
msgstr "បង្ហាញ​ប្រធាន​បទ​ជា​ចំណង​ជើង"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Displays the topic of the current channel in the window "
"caption.</action> If not selected, the topic is only displayed inside the "
"window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dock passive popups"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:484
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option is only available if Dock in system tray is checked. If it checked, "
"the passive popups will be displayed docked to the system tray."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid "One line text entry box"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:489
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is not selected, the entry box where you write your text in each "
"channel will expand on several lines depending of the text length. If this is "
"selected, only one line will be used and that means you will not see the "
"beginning of the text you are writing if it is longer than the line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid "History Length"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Stores up to this many lines of chat from each window, allowing you to scroll "
"upwards and see what has already been said."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto save history"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is selected, private message history is saved. When you open a private "
"window the second time with the same user, you will see a log (the history) of "
"your previous chat with him."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid "Per Channel Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:514
#, no-c-format
msgid "Override existing channels options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is selected, the settings in this tab will override each channel "
"options so these settings will be applied in each channel, independently of "
"your channel settings in the Channel menu. This setting will only work until "
"next time you open the configuration dialog and it will be reset unchecked "
"then. This is because you probably don't want to override the existing channels "
"options all the time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Time Stamp</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Prepends each thing said in the channel with the time it was "
"said,</action> in the form [HH:MM:SS]."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:526
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show topic"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid "Displays the channel topic on top of each channel window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:531
#, no-c-format
msgid "Beep on change"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If selected, a system beep will be generated whenever a user on your <command>"
"/notify</command> list signs onto the &irc; server you are on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:538
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable logging"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Creates log files for each channel per day. These log files are stored in "
"$KDEHOME/share/apps/ksirc/logs/ and the files look like: "
"/$KDEHOME/share/apps/ksirc/logs/#channelname_year_month_day_servername.log"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hide part/join messages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid "Don't show part/join messages. This is useful in a channel with many people."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default encoding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:549
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Fixes the default encoding for all channels. Choose the encoding in the "
"drop-down list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Startup</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can configure &ksirc;'s startup settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Server</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid "Name Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:582
#, no-c-format
msgid "Nick Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set your &irc; nickname."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid "Alternative Nick"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set the nickname to use if your first choice is already in use by another user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid "Real Name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:594 index.docbook:600
#, no-c-format
msgid "Your real name, as returned by a <command>/whois</command> query on you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:599
#, no-c-format
msgid "User ID"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:609
#, no-c-format
msgid "Notify List"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:611
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can enter a list of users who you want added to your <command>"
"/notify</command> list at startup. You will be alerted when each of the users "
"in the list is online."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Colors</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can configure &ksirc;'s use of color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:626
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Chat colors</guilabel> Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:627
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can set colors for each of the types of text. Clicking the color "
"button to the right of each text type's label will display a color selector box "
"in which you can choose the color in which you want this type of text to be "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid "Nick Colors"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:637
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Foreground:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Background:</guilabel> "
"set the colors for the foreground and background of users' nicknames in chat "
"windows. The <guilabel>Color for messages containing your nick:</guilabel> "
"option sets the color for any message appearing in a channel which contains "
"your nickname."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:646
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color codes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can set whether &ksirc; allows native color codes (see <xref "
"linkend=\"sectcolors\"/>) and also whether &mirc; color codes are allowed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:661
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>User Menu</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:662
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page allows configuration for the RMB (Right Mouse Button) menu for the "
"nick list located on the right in each channel. When you right click on a "
"nickname, some actions are defined by default. These are the actions listed on "
"the left. You can change these actions order, delete some and add others."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:667
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Server/Channel</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:668
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here are listed the servers and channels you join to using the New Server "
"(<keycap>F2</keycap>) and New Channel (<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>"
"N</keycap></keycombo>) dialogs via the Channel menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:671
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Server</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:672
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You add there the servers you want to use. Write the server name in the field "
"and click the Add Server to List button. If you want to delete a server from "
"the list, you click on the server name and then on the Delete Server from List "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:676
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You add there the channels you want to connect to. Write the channel name in "
"the field and click the Add Channel to List button. If you want to delete a "
"channel from the list, you click on the channel name and then on the Delete "
"Channel from List button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:681
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Auto Connect</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:685
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto Connect Setup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:686
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You set here the server and channels names that you want to connect directly "
"when KSirc starts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:687
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You need to use the Auto Connect Setup dialog first to add new channels. You "
"enter there the server name. The server port is set by default for most "
"servers. If you are not sure, just leave it as it is. Usually servers don't ask "
"for passwords so if you don't have a password, leave the Password field empty. "
"Then add a channel name and click the Add button. The channel will be displayed "
"in the Auto Connect List."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:688
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to add more channel for a same server, click on the server in the "
"Auto Connect List and the server name will be displayed in the Auto Connect "
"Setup dialog. Write the channel name in the Channel field and click on "
"Update/Add."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:691
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to remove a channel form the Auto Connect List, click on the channel "
"name in the list and then click the Delete button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:698
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Fonts</guilabel> Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:699
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change here the font for the main window. Select the font you want then "
"click the Apply button to preview the change. Ok applies the changes and quits "
"the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:724
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ksirc; Colors"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:726
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ksirc; follows the color scheme used by &mirc; and a slight modification for "
"more powerful in house use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:730
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;fg&gt; == foreground\n"
"&lt;bg&gt; == background\n"
"&lsqb;&rsqb; == optional"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:733
#, no-c-format
msgid "&mirc; compatibility"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:735 index.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid "Format:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:738
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>0x03&lt;fg&gt;&lsqb;,&lt;bg&gt;&rsqb;</userinput> "
"sets the foreground and background"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:742
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>0x03</userinput> resets to defaults for <emphasis>that</emphasis> "
"line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:749
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ksirc; native"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:755
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>&tilde;&lt;fg&gt;&lsqb;,&lt;bg&gt;&rsqb;</userinput> "
"sets the foreground and background"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:759
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>&tilde;c</userinput> resets to defaults"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:762
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>&tilde;b</userinput> sets bold font"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:765
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>&tilde;u</userinput> sets underline"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:768
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>&tilde;i</userinput> sets italics"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:771
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>&tilde;r</userinput> sets reverse video"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:775
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Why did I change &ksirc; to use &tilde; instead of 0x03 (<keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo>"
")? Well, it's hard to use 0x03 in scripts and not all C functions seem to like "
"it. <userinput>&tilde;<replaceable>letter</replaceable></userinput> "
"also allows more commands while not stomping on &mirc;'s future changes."
msgstr ""

