#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1290
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto identify"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you intend to use &irc; on a regular basis you will probably want to "
"register your nickname. This protects your nickname so that only you can use "
"it. On DALnet, after you log on, you register your nickname using the command "
"<userinput><command>/msg</command> nickserv register <replaceable>"
"PASSWORD</replaceable></userinput>, where <replaceable>PASSWORD</replaceable> "
"is your password. You'll get a confirmation your nickname has been registered."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then each time you log on to DALnet you get a message asking you to identify "
"yourself. You will then need to type <userinput><command>"
"/msg nickserv identify <replaceable>PASSWORD</replaceable></command></userinput>"
"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ksirc; can identify you automatically when you log into any channel. You "
"simply need to add the following Perl script in your home directory:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following script will work on Freenode. This script should be saved as "
"<filename>.sircrc.pl</filename> in your home directory. When you run &ksirc;, "
"this script will automatically have you identified."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:1321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"sub hook_nick_notice {\n"
"my $n = shift;\n"
"my $m = shift;\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"if($who =~ /NickServ/){\n"
"if($m =~ /If this is your nickname/){\n"
"$silent = 1; \n"
"&amp;msg(\"nickserv\", \"identify <replaceable>XXXXXX</replaceable>\");\n"
"$silent = 0; \n"
"}\n"
"}\n"
"}\n"
"&amp;addhook(\"notice\", \"nick_notice\");   # join on the \"end of MOTD\" "
"numeric"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1322
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace <replaceable>XXXXXX</replaceable> with your password."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The above script will work on other networks than Freenode where nickserv sends "
"you the request \"identify\" but on some networks like Undernet you will need "
"the following script:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:1332
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"sub hook_connected {\n"
"if($server =~ /undernet.org$/){\n"
"        &amp;msg(\"X\\@channels.undernet.org\", \"login <replaceable>"
"YOUR_NAME</replaceable> <replaceable>XXXX</replaceable>\");\n"
"                &amp;docommand(\"umode +x\");\n"
"}\n"
"}\n"
"&amp;addhook(\"255\", \"connected\");   # join on the \"end of MOTD\" numeric"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1334
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Replace <replaceable>YOUR_NAME</replaceable> with your login name and "
"<replaceable>XXXXXX</replaceable> with your password."
msgstr ""

